\taxon{Remark}
\title{Architecture coordinates relevant to post-training}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{transformer}
\tag{post-training}

\p{The next-token law hides several costs. Hidden width and block count affect
the work of one forward or backward pass. Attention structure affects how
that work grows with context length. The output head fixes the map through
which token-level losses reach the final hidden states.}

\p{These observations identify possible variables for later results. They do
not show that any one variable controls post-training gain. A theorem that
uses an architecture property must name the property and the computational
model in which its cost is measured.}
